---
/**
 * The strongest AAMP material in the corpus, and the clearest structural
 * difference between the two stacks: AdCP has no negotiation protocol at all.
 *
 * Every number below is read from seller-agent/docs/integration/negotiation.md
 * and docs/api/quotes.md. The plan requires all FOUR tier rows — an earlier
 * draft elsewhere printed three.
 */
import BaseLayout from '@agenticbrief/shared-ui/BaseLayout.astro'
import AnswerBox from '@agenticbrief/shared-ui/AnswerBox.astro'
import FaqBlock from '@agenticbrief/shared-ui/FaqBlock.astro'
import SpecSource from '@agenticbrief/shared-ui/SpecSource.astro'
import { aamp, adcp } from '@agenticbrief/protocol-data'
import {
  graph,
  organizationNode,
  personNode,
  webSiteNode,
  webPageNode,
  articleNode,
  breadcrumbNode,
  faqPageNode,
} from '@agenticbrief/seo/schema'
import { BASE, HUB } from '../lib/site'

const SELLER = 'https://github.com/IABTechLab/seller-agent/blob/main/docs'

const TIERS = [
  {
    tier: 'public',
    strategy: 'aggressive',
    rounds: 3,
    perRound: '3%',
    total: '8%',
    gapShare: '30%',
  },
  { tier: 'seat', strategy: 'standard', rounds: 4, perRound: '4%', total: '12%', gapShare: '40%' },
  {
    tier: 'agency',
    strategy: 'collaborative',
    rounds: 5,
    perRound: '5%',
    total: '15%',
    gapShare: '50%',
  },
  {
    tier: 'advertiser',
    strategy: 'premium',
    rounds: 6,
    perRound: '6%',
    total: '20%',
    gapShare: '65%',
  },
]

const TRUST = ['unknown', 'registered', 'approved', 'preferred', 'blocked']

const path = '/negotiation/'
const url = `${BASE}${path}`
const title = 'Quote, negotiate, book — price negotiation in AAMP'
const description =
  'AAMP is the only agentic advertising stack that specifies price negotiation between agents: four actions, tier-keyed concession caps, and a 24-hour quote TTL. AdCP has no equivalent.'
const answer =
  'AAMP specifies multi-round price negotiation between buyer and seller agents. A buyer requests a non-binding quote with a 24-hour TTL, then both sides exchange counters bounded by per-round and cumulative concession caps keyed to the buyer’s access tier.'

const faq = [
  {
    question: 'Does AdCP have a negotiation protocol?',
    answer: `No. Across all ${adcp.tasks.length} operations in AdCP ${adcp.version} there is no counter-offer, no quote object and no concession model. An AdCP buyer discovers products and creates a media buy; price is a property of the product, not something the two agents converge on.`,
  },
  {
    question: 'What are the four negotiation actions?',
    answer:
      'accept, counter, final_offer and reject. Each round records the buyer price, the seller price, the action taken, the concession made in that round and the cumulative concession so far.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How long is a quote valid?',
    answer:
      'Twenty-four hours. After that the quote expires and retrieving it returns HTTP 410. Quotes are explicitly non-binding until converted into a deal.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is this a ratified specification?',
    answer:
      'No, and that qualification matters. This model is documented in the seller-agent reference implementation, not in a ratified IAB Tech Lab specification. It is what one implementation does, published openly, rather than something an implementer is obliged to match.',
  },
]

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'AAMP Explorer', url: `${BASE}/` },
  { name: 'Negotiation', url },
]

const jsonLd = graph([
  organizationNode(),
  personNode(),
  webSiteNode({ siteUrl: BASE, name: 'AAMP Explorer', description }),
  webPageNode({ url, siteUrl: BASE, title, description, breadcrumb: {} }),
  breadcrumbNode(url, breadcrumbs),
  articleNode({
    url,
    title,
    description,
    datePublished: '2026-08-09',
    technical: true,
    proficiencyLevel: 'Expert',
    keywords: ['agent to agent deal negotiation', 'aamp negotiation', 'agentic price negotiation'],
    citations: [`${SELLER}/integration/negotiation.md`, `${SELLER}/api/quotes.md`],
  }),
  faqPageNode(url, faq),
])
---

<BaseLayout
  site="aampexplorer"
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path={path}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  wide
  ogType="article"
  publishDate={new Date('2026-08-09')}
  keywords={['agent to agent deal negotiation', 'aamp negotiation']}
>
  <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <ol><li><a href="/">AAMP Explorer</a></li><li><span>Negotiation</span></li></ol>
  </nav>
  <h1>Price negotiation in AAMP</h1>
  <AnswerBox answer={answer} />

  <p>
    This is the most substantial thing in the AAMP corpus, and it has no counterpart in AdCP. It is
    also the clearest illustration of what the two stacks are each for: AdCP models a catalogue you
    buy from, AAMP models a conversation you haggle in.
  </p>

  <p>
    One qualification, stated up front because it changes how much weight the numbers below can
    carry: this model lives in the <strong>seller-agent reference implementation</strong>, not in a
    ratified specification. It is what one implementation does and publishes, not a conformance
    requirement.
  </p>

  <h2>How does an AAMP negotiation run?</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>The buyer requests <strong>avails</strong> against the seller's media kit.</li>
    <li>
      The seller issues a <strong>quote</strong> — a non-binding price offer with a 24-hour TTL.
    </li>
    <li>
      Either side may <strong>counter</strong>. Each round is recorded with both prices, the action,
      and the concession made.
    </li>
    <li>
      The exchange ends on <code>accept</code>, <code>reject</code>, a <code>final_offer</code> that is
      accepted or refused, or the round limit.
    </li>
    <li>
      An accepted quote is converted into a <strong>deal</strong>, and the seller issues the deal
      ID. The sell side is the system of record.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What bounds the negotiation?</h2>
  <p>
    Concessions are capped, and the caps are keyed to the buyer's access tier. A buyer with no
    relationship gets three rounds and eight percent; a named advertiser gets six rounds and twenty.
  </p>

  <figure class="comparison">
    <table>
      <caption
        >Negotiation strategy by access tier, from seller-agent docs/integration/negotiation.md</caption
      >
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Access tier</th>
          <th scope="col">Strategy</th>
          <th scope="col">Max rounds</th>
          <th scope="col">Per-round cap</th>
          <th scope="col">Total cap</th>
          <th scope="col">Buyer gap share</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          TIERS.map((t) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">
                <code>{t.tier}</code>
              </th>
              <td>
                <code>{t.strategy}</code>
              </td>
              <td>{t.rounds}</td>
              <td>{t.perRound}</td>
              <td>{t.total}</td>
              <td>{t.gapShare}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </figure>

  <h2>How does a buyer get a better tier?</h2>
  <p>
    Not by claiming one. A buyer's effective tier is the minimum of the tier it claims and the
    ceiling its trust status allows, so identity alone does not buy a discount. Trust status runs
    {' '}{
      TRUST.map((t, i) => (
        <>
          {i > 0 && ' → '}
          <code>{t}</code>
        </>
      ))
    }, where <code>registered</code>
    {' '}means the agent was found in the AAMP registry.
  </p>

  <h2>Why does AdCP have nothing like this?</h2>
  <p>
    Because it models a different transaction. In AdCP {adcp.version}, a product carries its pricing
    options and a buyer either buys it or does not. There is no object representing an offer under
    discussion. Whether that is a gap or a deliberate scope boundary is exactly the kind of question
    the two camps have not published a joint answer to — and neither corpus references the other.
  </p>

  <FaqBlock entries={faq} />

  <h2>Related</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/repos/seller-agent/">The seller agent, where this model is implemented</a></li>
    <li>
      <a href="/repos/iab-agentic-primitives/">The wire contract these objects are defined in</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://adtechglossary.noetis.dev/negotiation/" rel="noopener"
        >Negotiation vocabulary, term by term</a
      >
    </li>
    <li><a href={`${HUB}/protocols/adcp-vs-aamp/`} rel="noopener">AdCP compared with AAMP</a></li>
  </ul>

  <SpecSource
    provenance={{
      repo: 'https://github.com/IABTechLab/seller-agent',
      commit: aamp.components.find((c) => c.name === 'seller-agent')?.commit ?? '',
      parsedAt: aamp.provenance.parsedAt,
      sourcePath: 'docs/integration/negotiation.md',
      sourceUrl: `${SELLER}/integration/negotiation.md`,
    }}
  />
</BaseLayout>
